From: thor2002ro <thor2002ro@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Local: media: cedrus: pad H616/H618 H.264 deblock storage

Wide H.264 pictures need more deblock storage than the generic estimate provides. A short buffer can overlap adjacent state.

Use the vendor margin for H616 and H618. Smaller pictures keep their current allocation.

Signed-off-by: thor2002ro <thor2002ro@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h264.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h264.c
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h264.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h264.c
@@ -683,8 +683,12 @@
 		 * are taken from CedarX source.
 		 */
 
-		ctx->codec.h264.deblk_buf_size =
-			ALIGN(ctx->src_fmt.width, 32) * 12;
+		if (ctx->codec.h264.h616)
+			ctx->codec.h264.deblk_buf_size =
+				DIV_ROUND_UP(ctx->src_fmt.width, 16) * 192 + 5952;
+		else
+			ctx->codec.h264.deblk_buf_size =
+				ALIGN(ctx->src_fmt.width, 32) * 12;
 		ctx->codec.h264.deblk_buf =
 			dma_alloc_attrs(dev->dev,
 					ctx->codec.h264.deblk_buf_size,
